  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-navigator-appversion says\r\n\r\n> Must return either the string \"4\\.0\" or a string representing the version of the browser in detail, e\\.g\\. \"1\\.0 \\(VMS; en\\-US\\) Mellblomenator/9000\"\\.\r\n\r\nAFAICT, all major browsers these days return a string that starts with `5.0 (` (with more or less stuff after), so perhaps the spec should require that the return value start with those characters or at least not suggest `4.0` or starting with `1.0 (`.\r\n\r\nIf appears that in WebKit and Blink, `navigator.appVersion` is the same as `navigator.userAgent` with the prefix `Mozilla/` removed. In Gecko, it appears to be one of `5.0 (X11)`, `5.0 (Macintosh)`, `5.0 (Windows)`, or `5.0 (Android)`. Given that https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-navigator-compatibility-mode exists, perhaps the spec could even require what the previous sentence says.",
